House Republicans are considering  whether to force a vote on a resolution  to impeach Deputy Attorney General rod  Rosenstein 11 house conservatives  introduced articles of impeachment  yesterday they accused Rosen Stein who  oversees the special council's Russia  investigation of not being responsive  enough to their requests for documents  no word if that's grounds for  impeachment Paula Reid is at the White  House Paula good morning good morning  this is just the latest in this ongoing  feud between the president's Republican  allies and the Justice Department  now Tea Party leaders mark meadows of  North Carolina and Jim Jordan of Ohio  along with nine others are steering this  effort to try to oust Rosenstein they're  alleging that he has conflicts of  interest in the ongoing Special Counsel  investigation they also accuse him of  intentionally withholding documents in  other ongoing investigations into the  Justice Department and how it handled  investigations related to the 2016  elections now if Rosenstein was  impeached the Russian investigation  would continue but Special Counsel  Muller he would be supervised by a  different senior Justice Department  official Rosenstein has pushed back  against these partisan attacks warning  back in May that the Justice Department  is quote not going to be extorted but  it's unclear how far they're actually  going to be able to get with this effort  or if it could even come to a vote  because several top Republican lawmakers  have said they do not support the idea  of trying to impeach Rosen Stein  including House Oversight Chair trey  Gowdy now the Justice Department has not  commented yet on these efforts Gail all  right thank you very much Paula
 

